& [Question]
  + what scaling claims can and cannot be made about the clean-replayed durable Identity Accounting Workspace

& [ObservedStorageShape]
  + AccountingJournal retains every event and exactly one complete IdentityLedger for every event successor
  + each IdentityLedger retains every current AccountableObject in the basket even when one object changed
  + every AdmissionApplied event retains the complete AccountableObjectAdmission including its complete FacultyCycle
  + SnapshotStore persists each succeeding AccountingJournal as a separate content-named complete canonical JSON file
  + restart scans snapshots validates each complete journal chooses one unique maximal history and requires every other history to be its exact prefix
  + configured maximum snapshot bytes and maximum snapshot count bound failure but do not change the representation

& [AsymptoticAssessment]
  + let H be event count B average complete ledger bytes and A average retained event payload bytes
  + one latest journal snapshot is approximately order H times B plus H times A because every generation retains a complete ledger and event
  + retaining every prefix snapshot makes cumulative store bytes approximately order H squared times B plus H squared times A in the absence of filesystem-level deduplication
  + admission events can be materially larger than patches because they retain the complete seven-faculty Judgment record
  + restart validation replays every event and validates every retained ledger in every scanned candidate so startup work also grows with retained history volume
  + these are structural growth observations and not measured throughput latency capacity or cost results

& [CurrentFitness]
  + excellent for bounded local experiments exact replay adversarial validation crash-recoverable custody and proving semantics before optimization
  + suitable when basket history snapshot count and total bytes remain under explicit configured limits
  + unsuitable as evidence that one process or one approximately four-thousand-dollar node can host any asserted number of high-demand or low-demand community users
  + no user-capacity estimate is supportable without workload model model-serving budget concurrency latency context size event rate storage growth and fault-tolerance measurements

& [NearTermMeasurement]
  + generate deterministic baskets across object counts 10 100 1000 and representative object-body sizes
  + apply patch-heavy admission-heavy and mixed workloads across increasing event counts
  + measure latest snapshot bytes cumulative store bytes persist latency restart latency validation latency peak memory and refusal threshold
  + run cold and warm filesystem conditions and record hardware filesystem build profile and exact commit
  + compare observed curves to the structural model before selecting a replacement representation

& [LikelyProductionDirection]
  + preserve event and ledger semantic identities while storing immutable content-addressed object records relation records events and ledger manifests as separately deduplicated blobs
  + let each generation manifest reference unchanged object digests rather than copy complete bodies
  + append one canonical event plus successor manifest atomically and periodically create signed or independently validated checkpoints
  + restore from checkpoint plus bounded event suffix while retaining whole-history verification and fork detection
  + use garbage collection only under a separately governed retention policy because prefix evidence must not disappear silently
  + keep the current complete JSON snapshot codec as a portable export proof fixture and recovery oracle even if it is not the serving representation

& [ConsistencyWithP6]
  + P6 compact inference manifests solve prompt-surface scaling and do not solve durable-history scaling
  + content-addressed manifest storage could later reuse P6 identity summary concepts but must not couple read-only attention receipts to journal state
  + P6 should remain bounded and clean-replayed before storage redesign to avoid mixing inference protocol and persistence representation changes

& [DeploymentGuardrail]
  + advertise this store as experimental bounded local custody until benchmark evidence and a service-level workload contract exist
  + reject before configured capacity rather than deleting history compacting without proof or claiming transparent scale
  + separate LLM token generation capacity from identity-accounting request capacity because they have different bottlenecks

& [Nonclaims]
  + no benchmark was executed and no exact asymptotic coefficient throughput user count monthly price or hardware fitness is claimed
  + filesystem compression deduplication cache and antivirus effects were not measured
  + no production storage implementation migration deletion or publication is authorized

& [RecommendedSequence]
  + complete P6 and behavioral identity evaluation
  + implement a deterministic durability benchmark before any community-node capacity estimate
  + form storage P8 only from measured bottlenecks while preserving P5 semantics and clean portable export
